# Normalize Python sources to LF (FIX-242 R0 P3-2).
#
# Evidence (2026-08-07, `git ls-files --eol`): the repository index is
# already 100% LF (556/556 files i/lf); core.autocrlf=true leaves mixed
# working-tree line endings on Windows (a snapshot counted 28 .py files
# with CRLF/mixed endings; non-.py files vary over time). Locking *.py to
# eol=lf makes working-tree line endings deterministic for Python sources
# without renormalizing any committed content (zero commit diff — the
# index stays LF).
*.py text eol=lf
# Lock JSON sources to LF too (FIX-250): without this, core.autocrlf=true
# leaves core/releases/*.json as CRLF stat noise (git reports "M" with zero
# content diff). The index is already LF — renormalizing is zero commit diff.
*.json text eol=lf
